@anon.e792752b4454889dead1a66caae2c60f.1387 = private unnamed_addr constant [1159 x i8] c"Whether to use Google-style, NumPy-style conventions, or the [PEP 257](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/) defaults when analyzing docstring sections.\0A\0AEnabling a convention will disable all rules that are not included in the specified convention. As such, the intended workflow is to enable a convention and then selectively enable or disable any additional rules on top of it.\0A\0AFor example, to use Google-style conventions but avoid requiring documentation for every function parameter:\0A\0A```toml [tool.ruff.lint] # Enable all `pydocstyle` rules, limiting to those that adhere to the # Google convention via `convention = \22google\22`, below. select = [\22D\22]\0A\0A# On top of the Google convention, disable `D417`, which requires # documentation for every function parameter. ignore = [\22D417\22]\0A\0A[tool.ruff.lint.pydocstyle] convention = \22google\22 ```\0A\0ATo enable an additional rule that's excluded from the convention, select the desired rule via its fully qualified rule code (e.g., `D400` instead of `D4` or `D40`):\0A\0A```toml [tool.ruff.lint] # Enable D400 on top of the Google convention. extend-select = [\22D400\22]\0A\0A[tool.ruff.lint.pydocstyle] convention = \22google\22 ```", align 1
