@anon.e792752b4454889dead1a66caae2c60f.1556 = private unnamed_addr constant [1549 x i8] c"Whether to format code snippets in docstrings.\0A\0AWhen this is enabled, Python code examples within docstrings are\0Aautomatically reformatted.\0A\0AFor example, when this is enabled, the following code:\0A\0A```python\0Adef f(x):\0A    \22\22\22\0A    Something about `f`. And an example in doctest format:\0A\0A    >>> f(  x  )\0A\0A    Markdown is also supported:\0A\0A    ```py\0A    f(  x  )\0A    ```\0A\0A    As are reStructuredText literal blocks::\0A\0A        f(  x  )\0A\0A\0A    And reStructuredText code blocks:\0A\0A    .. code-block:: python\0A\0A        f(  x  )\0A    \22\22\22\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0A... will be reformatted (assuming the rest of the options are set to\0Atheir defaults) as:\0A\0A```python\0Adef f(x):\0A    \22\22\22\0A    Something about `f`. And an example in doctest format:\0A\0A    >>> f(x)\0A\0A    Markdown is also supported:\0A\0A    ```py\0A    f(x)\0A    ```\0A\0A    As are reStructuredText literal blocks::\0A\0A        f(x)\0A\0A\0A    And reStructuredText code blocks:\0A\0A    .. code-block:: python\0A\0A        f(x)\0A    \22\22\22\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0AIf a code snippet in a docstring contains invalid Python code or if the\0Aformatter would otherwise write invalid Python code, then the code\0Aexample is ignored by the formatter and kept as-is.\0A\0ACurrently, doctest, Markdown, reStructuredText literal blocks, and\0AreStructuredText code blocks are all supported and automatically\0Arecognized. In the case of unlabeled fenced code blocks in Markdown and\0AreStructuredText literal blocks, the contents are assumed to be Python\0Aand reformatted. As with any other format, if the contents aren't valid\0APython, then the block is left untouched automatically.", align 1
@anon.e792752b4454889dead1a66caae2c60f.1558 = private unnamed_addr constant [82 x i8] c"# Enable reformatting of code snippets in docstrings.\0Adocstring-code-format = true", align 1
