@anon.e792752b4454889dead1a66caae2c60f.1561 = private unnamed_addr constant [1564 x i8] c"Set the line length used when formatting code snippets in docstrings.\0A\0AThis only has an effect when the `docstring-code-format` setting is\0Aenabled.\0A\0AThe default value for this setting is `\22dynamic\22`, which has the effect\0Aof ensuring that any reformatted code examples in docstrings adhere to\0Athe global line length configuration that is used for the surrounding\0APython code. The point of this setting is that it takes the indentation\0Aof the docstring into account when reformatting code examples.\0A\0AAlternatively, this can be set to a fixed integer, which will result\0Ain the same line length limit being applied to all reformatted code\0Aexamples in docstrings. When set to a fixed integer, the indent of the\0Adocstring is not taken into account. That is, this may result in lines\0Ain the reformatted code example that exceed the globally configured\0Aline length limit.\0A\0AFor example, when this is set to `20` and [`docstring-code-format`](#docstring-code-format)\0Ais enabled, then this code:\0A\0A```python\0Adef f(x):\0A    '''\0A    Something about `f`. And an example:\0A\0A    .. code-block:: python\0A\0A        foo, bar, quux = this_is_a_long_line(lion, hippo, lemur, bear)\0A    '''\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0A... will be reformatted (assuming the rest of the options are set\0Ato their defaults) as:\0A\0A```python\0Adef f(x):\0A    \22\22\22\0A    Something about `f`. And an example:\0A\0A    .. code-block:: python\0A\0A        (\0A            foo,\0A            bar,\0A            quux,\0A        ) = this_is_a_long_line(\0A            lion,\0A            hippo,\0A            lemur,\0A            bear,\0A        )\0A    \22\22\22\0A    pass\0A```", align 1
